ntdll: tell the JS host about each image view (docs/design/wine-unix.md,
section 6, "Images (M3)"; abi.md v5, the import tw_image_mapped).

Why: JS links an image's AOT module before any of its code runs, and finds
the module by the image file's path, its sha256 and the base.

- virtual_map_image (virtual.c): once the view is mapped and relocated
  (map_image_into_view, L3420, relocates it to the server's map address,
  L3205-3223) and the server has recorded it, it calls
  tw_image_mapped(unix_fd, base, size), with the base and size it returns
  to its caller (L3442-3448). unix_fd, the image file's, is still open
  there: it is closed only at the end (L3453).
- Every image comes through here: NtMapViewOfSection of a SEC_IMAGE
  section and the loader's builtin modules (virtual_map_builtin_module).

Invalidation, the other half of section 6, needs no change here: every
unmap and every fixed map over a range reaches the backend's tw_munmap or
tw_mmap, which call tw_invalidate (native/wine/src/virtual_wasm.c).

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -107,6 +107,9 @@
 #define mprotect tw_mprotect
 #define madvise tw_madvise
 #define msync tw_msync
+/* The JS host links the image's AOT module (abi.md v5, "Host entries of the
+ * Unix side"; wine-unix.md, section 6, "Images"). */
+void tw_image_mapped( int fd, UINT64 base, UINT64 size );
 #endif
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(virtual);
@@ -3632,6 +3635,10 @@
         *addr_ptr = view->base;
         *size_ptr = size;
         VIRTUAL_DEBUG_DUMP_VIEW( view );
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+        /* mapped and relocated; unix_fd is still the image file's */
+        tw_image_mapped( unix_fd, (UINT_PTR)view->base, size );
+#endif
     }
     else delete_view( view );
 
